# What does NOT get uploaded to Cloud Build.
#
# Written out rather than left implicit. With no file here gcloud generates one
# from .gitignore, which would in fact exclude the right things today, but the
# workbook in data/raw carries blueprint owner names and email addresses and
# that is not a thing to protect by side effect of another file.
#
# The same reasoning as `run.py package`, which builds its zip from a list
# rather than by walking a folder. The Dockerfile is the third layer: it copies
# app and renderer by name, so even an upload carrying more than it should
# could not put it in the image.

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# The extract's source, and the key.
data/raw/
.env

# Nothing here belongs in a build.
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tests/
docs/
deploy/
*.zip
NW Digital City.html
*.png
run.cmd
run.sh
requirements-dev.txt
